§ `Section 21(2): the name of a corporation with an English and a French form`

-- Plain gloss: where an enactment establishes a corporation and each version of the enactment gives the name only in the form of that
-- version's own language, the name of the corporation is the form in each version.
-- src:162 | (2) Where an enactment establishes a corporation and in each of the English and French versions of the enactment the name of the corporation is in the form only of the language of that version, the name of the corporation shall consist of the form of its name in each of the versions of the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 21(2) (src:162)
GIVEN `the name in the English version` IS A STRING
      `the name in the French version` IS A STRING
      `each version gives the name only in the form of its own language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the name of a corporation an enactment establishes, with` `the name in the English version` `in the English version and` `the name in the French version` `in the French version, where` `each version gives the name only in the form of its own language` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `each version gives the name only in the form of its own language` THEN LIST `the name in the English version`, `the name in the French version`
           OTHERWISE `section 21(2) speaks of a name given in each version only in the form of that version's language and says nothing of any other`

-- src:162 | (2) Where an enactment establishes a corporation and in each of the English and French versions of the enactment the name of the corporation is in the form only of the language of that version, the name of the corporation shall consist of the form of its name in each of the versions of the enactment.
@ref Interpretation Act s 21(2) (src:162)
