    REFUSE "section 21(2) speaks of a name given in each version only in the form of that version's language and says nothing of any other"

§ `Section 25(2): copies printed by the Queen's Printer`

-- Plain gloss: a copy of an enactment with what purports to be the name or title of the Queen's Printer and Controller of Stationery, or the
-- Queen's Printer, printed on it is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen's Printer for Canada.
-- FORK F-QUEENS: the text says "Queen's" while the Sovereign is a King.  Taken: a title styled for the reigning Sovereign counts, so the
-- King's Printer titles are listed with the Queen's.  The other reading lists only the titles the text prints.
-- src:211 | (2) Every copy of an enactment having printed thereon what purports to be the name or title of the Queen’s Printer and Controller of Stationery or the Queen’s Printer is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen’s Printer for Canada.
@ref Interpretation Act s 25(2) (src:211)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the titles that section 25(2) names, with the titles styled for the reigning Sovereign` MEANS
    LIST "the Queen’s Printer and Controller of Stationery"
       , "the Queen’s Printer"
       , "the King’s Printer and Controller of Stationery"
       , "the King’s Printer"

-- src:211 | (2) Every copy of an enactment having printed thereon what purports to be the name or title of the Queen’s Printer and Controller of Stationery or the Queen’s Printer is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen’s Printer for Canada.
@ref Interpretation Act s 25(2) (src:211)
GIVEN `the name or title printed on the copy` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a copy of an enactment is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen's Printer for Canada, when it has printed on it` `the name or title printed on the copy` MEANS
    BRANCH IF elem `the name or title printed on the copy` `the titles that section 25(2) names, with the titles styled for the reigning Sovereign`
        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE `section 25(2) names two titles and does not say what is made of a copy that bears another`

-- src:211 | (2) Every copy of an enactment having printed thereon what purports to be the name or title of the Queen’s Printer and Controller of Stationery or the Queen’s Printer is deemed to be a copy purporting to be printed by the Queen’s Printer for Canada.
@ref Interpretation Act s 25(2) (src:211)
