    REFUSE "section 25(2) names two titles and does not say what is made of a copy that bears another"

§ `Section 33: gender, number and grammatical forms`

-- Plain gloss: words that import female persons include male persons and corporations, and words that import male persons include female
-- persons and corporations.  The singular includes the plural and the plural the singular.  Where a word is defined, its other parts of
-- speech and grammatical forms have corresponding meanings.
-- src:248 | 33 (1) Words importing female persons include male persons and corporations and words importing male persons include female persons and corporations.
@ref Interpretation Act s 33(1) (src:248)
GIVEN i IS A `What a word imports`
      x IS A `What a word imports`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words importing` i `include those importing` x MEANS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `female persons` THEN
        CONSIDER x
        WHEN `female persons` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `male persons`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `corporations`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `something else` THEN `section 33(1) speaks of words importing female or male persons and says nothing of any other`
    WHEN `male persons` THEN
        CONSIDER x
        WHEN `female persons` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `male persons`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `corporations`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `something else` THEN `section 33(1) speaks of words importing female or male persons and says nothing of any other`
    WHEN `corporations`   THEN `section 33(1) speaks of words importing female or male persons and says nothing of any other`
    WHEN `something else` THEN `section 33(1) speaks of words importing female or male persons and says nothing of any other`

-- src:248 | 33 (1) Words importing female persons include male persons and corporations and words importing male persons include female persons and corporations.
@ref Interpretation Act s 33(1) (src:248)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 33(1) speaks of words importing female or male persons and says nothing of any other` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 33(1) speaks of words importing female or male persons and says nothing of any other"

-- src:250 | (2) Words in the singular include the plural, and words in the plural include the singular.
@ref Interpretation Act s 33(2) (src:250)
GIVEN n IS A `A grammatical number`
      m IS A `A grammatical number`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words in` n `include words in` m MEANS
    TRUE

-- src:252 | (3) Where a word is defined, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the same word have corresponding meanings.
@ref Interpretation Act s 33(3) (src:252)
GIVEN f IS A `A form of a word`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a form of a defined word has a corresponding meaning` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `the word as defined`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another part of speech of the word defined`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another grammatical form of the word defined` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a different word`                             THEN `section 33(3) speaks of other forms of the same word and says nothing of a different word`

-- src:252 | (3) Where a word is defined, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the same word have corresponding meanings.
@ref Interpretation Act s 33(3) (src:252)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 33(3) speaks of other forms of the same word and says nothing of a different word` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 33(3) speaks of other forms of the same word and says nothing of a different word"

§ `Section 36: telegraph`

-- Plain gloss: the expression "telegraph" and its derivatives, in an enactment or in an Act of a provincial legislature enacted before the
-- province became part of Canada on a subject within the legislative powers of Parliament, are deemed not to include "telephone" or its
-- derivatives.
DECLARE `Where the expression telegraph is used` IS ONE OF
    `in an enactment`
    `in an Act of a provincial legislature enacted before the province became part of Canada, on a subject within the legislative powers of Parliament`
    `in an Act of a provincial legislature enacted before the province became part of Canada, on a subject not within the legislative powers of Parliament`
    `somewhere else`

-- src:364 | 36 The expression telegraph and its derivatives, in an enactment or in an Act of the legislature of any province enacted before that province became part of Canada on any subject that is within the legislative powers of Parliament, are deemed not to include the word “telephone” or its derivatives.
@ref Interpretation Act s 36 (src:364)
GIVEN w IS A `Where the expression telegraph is used`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the expression telegraph includes the word telephone, used` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `in an enactment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in an Act of a provincial legislature enacted before the province became part of Canada, on a subject within the legislative powers of Parliament` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `in an Act of a provincial legislature enacted before the province became part of Canada, on a subject not within the legislative powers of Parliament` THEN `section 36 speaks of enactments and of earlier provincial Acts on subjects within the powers of Parliament and says nothing of any other use`
    WHEN `somewhere else` THEN `section 36 speaks of enactments and of earlier provincial Acts on subjects within the powers of Parliament and says nothing of any other use`

-- src:364 | 36 The expression telegraph and its derivatives, in an enactment or in an Act of the legislature of any province enacted before that province became part of Canada on any subject that is within the legislative powers of Parliament, are deemed not to include the word “telephone” or its derivatives.
@ref Interpretation Act s 36 (src:364)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 36 speaks of enactments and of earlier provincial Acts on subjects within the powers of Parliament and says nothing of any other use` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 36 speaks of enactments and of earlier provincial Acts on subjects within the powers of Parliament and says nothing of any other use"

§ `Section 38: common names`

-- Plain gloss: the name commonly applied to any country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing
-- means the one to which the name is commonly applied, although the name is not its formal or extended designation.
-- src:373 | 38 The name commonly applied to any country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing means the country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing to which the name is commonly applied, although the name is not the formal or extended designation thereof.
@ref Interpretation Act s 38 (src:373)
GIVEN `the name is commonly applied to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is the formal or extended designation of the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the name means the thing to which it is commonly applied where` `the name is commonly applied to the thing` `whether or not` `the name is the formal or extended designation of the thing` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the name is commonly applied to the thing` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE `section 38 speaks of the name commonly applied and says nothing of a name not commonly applied`

-- src:373 | 38 The name commonly applied to any country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing means the country, place, body, corporation, society, officer, functionary, person, party or thing to which the name is commonly applied, although the name is not the formal or extended designation thereof.
@ref Interpretation Act s 38 (src:373)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 38 speaks of the name commonly applied and says nothing of a name not commonly applied` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 38 speaks of the name commonly applied and says nothing of a name not commonly applied"

§ `Section 40: citation of an enactment`

-- Plain gloss: an Act may be cited by its chapter number in the Revised Statutes, by its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year
-- or regnal year, or by its long title or short title.  A regulation may be cited by its long title or short title, by the Act under which it
-- was made, or by the number or designation under which the Clerk of the Privy Council registered it.  A citation of an enactment is deemed
-- to cite it as amended.
-- FORK F-40-2-DATE: "as amended" does not say as amended on what date.  Taken: as amended up to the date on which the citation is read and
-- applied, so a later amendment is counted once it has been made.  The other reading counts only the amendments made by the date the
-- citation was written.
-- src:386 | (a) an Act may be cited by reference to its chapter number in the Revised Statutes, by reference to its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted or by reference to its long title or short title, with or without reference to its chapter number; and
-- src:387 | (b) a regulation may be cited by reference to its long title or short title, by reference to the Act under which it was made or by reference to the number or designation under which it was registered by the Clerk of the Privy Council.
@ref Interpretation Act s 40(1)(a) (src:386) and s 40(1)(b) (src:387)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of instrument`
      w IS A `A way of citing an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is permitted to cite` k `in the way` w MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an Act of Parliament` THEN
        CONSIDER w
        WHEN `by its chapter number in the Revised Statutes` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by its long title`  THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by its short title` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by the Act under which it was made` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
        WHEN `by the number or designation under which it was registered by the Clerk of the Privy Council` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
        WHEN `by some other description` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
    WHEN `a regulation` THEN
        CONSIDER w
        WHEN `by its long title`  THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by its short title` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by the Act under which it was made` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by the number or designation under which it was registered by the Clerk of the Privy Council` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `by its chapter number in the Revised Statutes` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
        WHEN `by its chapter number in the volume of Acts for the year or regnal year in which it was enacted` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
        WHEN `by some other description` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
    WHEN `an Act of a legislature` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
    WHEN `a portion of an Act of Parliament` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
    WHEN `a portion of a regulation` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`
    WHEN `an instrument of none of these kinds` THEN `section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden`

-- src:385 | 40 (1) In an enactment or document,
@ref Interpretation Act s 40(1) (src:385)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 40(1) lists the ways of citing an Act and the ways of citing a regulation and does not say that another way is forbidden"

-- src:389 | (2) A citation of or reference to an enactment is deemed to be a citation of or reference to the enactment as amended.
@ref Interpretation Act s 40(2) (src:389)
GIVEN `the day the citation is read and applied` IS A DATE
      `the days on which the enactment was amended` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the amendments a citation of an enactment includes, read and applied on` `the day the citation is read and applied` `when the enactment was amended on` `the days on which the enactment was amended` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN d YIELD d <= `the day the citation is read and applied`) `the days on which the enactment was amended`

§ `Section 41(2): where a reference in an enactment points`

-- Plain gloss: a reference to a part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form is read as a reference to one of the enactment in which
-- it occurs.  A reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause or subclause is read as one of the section, subsection, paragraph,
-- subparagraph or clause in which it occurs.  A reference to regulations is read as one to regulations made under the enactment in which it
-- occurs.  A reference by number or letter to a division or line of another enactment is read as one to it as printed by authority of law.
-- src:393 | (2) A reference in an enactment to a part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form shall be read as a reference to a part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form of the enactment in which the reference occurs.
-- src:395 | (3) A reference in an enactment to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause or subclause shall be read as a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause or subclause of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs.
-- src:397 | (4) A reference in an enactment to regulations shall be read as a reference to regulations made under the enactment in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act s 41(2) (src:393), s 41(3) (src:395) and s 41(4) (src:397)
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of division referred to`
GIVETH A STRING
`the place a reference in an enactment points to, when it is a reference to` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a part`        THEN "a part of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a division`    THEN "a division of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a section`     THEN "a section of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a schedule`    THEN "a schedule of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `an appendix`   THEN "an appendix of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a form`        THEN "a form of the enactment in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a subsection`  THEN "a subsection of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a paragraph`   THEN "a paragraph of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a subparagraph` THEN "a subparagraph of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a clause`      THEN "a clause of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `a subclause`   THEN "a subclause of the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or clause, as the case may be, in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `regulations`   THEN "regulations made under the enactment in which the reference occurs"
    WHEN `anything else` THEN `section 41 says where a reference to a division, a subdivision, regulations or another enactment points and says nothing of any other reference`

-- src:399 | (5) A reference in an enactment by number or letter to any section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause or other division or line of another enactment shall be read as a reference to the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause or other division or line of such other enactment as printed by authority of law.
@ref Interpretation Act s 41(5) (src:399)
GIVEN `the reference is by number or letter to a section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause or other division or line of another enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`a reference to another enactment is read as a reference to the provision` `the reference is by number or letter to a section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause or other division or line of another enactment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the reference is by number or letter to a section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause or other division or line of another enactment`
        THEN "the section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, clause, subclause or other division or line of such other enactment as printed by authority of law"
        OTHERWISE `section 41 says where a reference to a division, a subdivision, regulations or another enactment points and says nothing of any other reference`

-- src:393 | (2) A reference in an enactment to a part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form shall be read as a reference to a part, division, section, schedule, appendix or form of the enactment in which the reference occurs.
@ref Interpretation Act s 41(2) (src:393)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 41 says where a reference to a division, a subdivision, regulations or another enactment points and says nothing of any other reference` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 41 says where a reference to a division, a subdivision, regulations or another enactment points and says nothing of any other reference"

§ `Section 42: repeal and amendment of an Act`

-- Plain gloss: every Act is construed as reserving to Parliament the power of repealing or amending it, and of revoking, restricting or
-- modifying a power, privilege or advantage it vests in or grants to a person.  An Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the
-- same session of Parliament.  An amending enactment is construed as part of the enactment it amends, as far as consistent with its tenor.
DECLARE `A thing Parliament may do to an Act` IS ONE OF
    `repeal the Act`
    `amend the Act`
    `revoke a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person`
    `restrict a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person`
    `modify a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person`
    `some other thing`

-- src:403 | 42 (1) Every Act shall be so construed as to reserve to Parliament the power of repealing or amending it, and of revoking, restricting or modifying any power, privilege or advantage thereby vested in or granted to any person.
@ref Interpretation Act s 42(1) (src:403)
GIVEN t IS A `A thing Parliament may do to an Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Parliament has reserved to itself the power to` t MEANS
    CONSIDER t
    WHEN `repeal the Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `amend the Act`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `revoke a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `restrict a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `modify a power, privilege or advantage that the Act vests in or grants to a person`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `some other thing` THEN `section 42(1) names five powers that are reserved and does not say whether any other thing is reserved`

-- src:403 | 42 (1) Every Act shall be so construed as to reserve to Parliament the power of repealing or amending it, and of revoking, restricting or modifying any power, privilege or advantage thereby vested in or granted to any person.
@ref Interpretation Act s 42(1) (src:403)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 42(1) names five powers that are reserved and does not say whether any other thing is reserved` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 42(1) names five powers that are reserved and does not say whether any other thing is reserved"

-- src:405 | (2) An Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session of Parliament.
@ref Interpretation Act s 42(2) (src:405)
GIVEN `the later Act was passed in the same session of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session where` `the later Act was passed in the same session of Parliament` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the later Act was passed in the same session of Parliament` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE `section 42(2) speaks of an Act passed in the same session and says nothing of one passed in another`

-- src:405 | (2) An Act may be amended or repealed by an Act passed in the same session of Parliament.
@ref Interpretation Act s 42(2) (src:405)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 42(2) speaks of an Act passed in the same session and says nothing of one passed in another` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 42(2) speaks of an Act passed in the same session and says nothing of one passed in another"

-- src:407 | (3) An amending enactment, as far as consistent with the tenor thereof, shall be construed as part of the enactment that it amends.
@ref Interpretation Act s 42(3) (src:407)
GIVEN `the provision is consistent with the tenor of the amending enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an amending enactment is construed as part of the enactment that it amends, so far as` `the provision is consistent with the tenor of the amending enactment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the provision is consistent with the tenor of the amending enactment` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE `section 42(3) construes an amending enactment as part of the enactment it amends so far as consistent with its tenor and says nothing of the rest`

-- src:407 | (3) An amending enactment, as far as consistent with the tenor thereof, shall be construed as part of the enactment that it amends.
@ref Interpretation Act s 42(3) (src:407)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 42(3) construes an amending enactment as part of the enactment it amends so far as consistent with its tenor and says nothing of the rest` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 42(3) construes an amending enactment as part of the enactment it amends so far as consistent with its tenor and says nothing of the rest"

§ `Section 45: what a repeal, an amendment or a re-enactment does not imply`

-- Plain gloss: the repeal of an enactment, in whole or in part, is not deemed to be or involve a declaration that it was previously in
-- force.  The amendment of an enactment is not deemed to be or involve a declaration that the law under it was different from the law as
-- amended.  Repeal or amendment is not deemed to involve any declaration as to the previous state of the law.  A re-enactment, revision,
-- consolidation or amendment is not deemed to be or involve an adoption of the construction placed on the language by judicial decision or
-- otherwise.  Each is stated as "shall not be deemed", so each answer here is FALSE; the cases the text does not name are refusals.
DECLARE `What is done to an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `repealing it in whole`
    `repealing it in part`
    `amending it`
    `re-enacting it`
    `revising it`
    `consolidating it`
    `something else`

DECLARE `What might be taken to follow from it` IS ONE OF
    `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force`
    `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended`
    `a declaration as to the previous state of the law`
    `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise`

-- src:430 | 45 (1) The repeal of an enactment in whole or in part shall not be deemed to be or to involve a declaration that the enactment was previously in force or was considered by Parliament or other body or person by whom the enactment was enacted to have been previously in force.
-- src:432 | (2) The amendment of an enactment shall not be deemed to be or to involve a declaration that the law under that enactment was or was considered by Parliament or other body or person by whom the enactment was enacted to have been different from the law as it is under the enactment as amended.
-- src:434 | (3) The repeal or amendment of an enactment in whole or in part shall not be deemed to be or to involve any declaration as to the previous state of the law.
-- src:436 | (4) A re-enactment, revision, consolidation or amendment of an enactment shall not be deemed to be or to involve an adoption of the construction that has by judicial decision or otherwise been placed on the language used in the enactment or on similar language.
@ref Interpretation Act s 45(1) (src:430), s 45(2) (src:432), s 45(3) (src:434) and s 45(4) (src:436)
GIVEN i IS A `What might be taken to follow from it`
      a IS A `What is done to an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is deemed to be or to involve` i `when the enactment is subject to` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `repealing it in whole` THEN
        CONSIDER i
        WHEN `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
    WHEN `repealing it in part` THEN
        CONSIDER i
        WHEN `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
    WHEN `amending it` THEN
        CONSIDER i
        WHEN `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `re-enacting it` THEN
        CONSIDER i
        WHEN `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
        WHEN `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
        WHEN `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
    WHEN `revising it` THEN
        CONSIDER i
        WHEN `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
        WHEN `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
        WHEN `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
    WHEN `consolidating it` THEN
        CONSIDER i
        WHEN `an adoption of the construction placed on the language used, or on similar language, by judicial decision or otherwise` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a declaration that the enactment was previously in force` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
        WHEN `a declaration that the law under the enactment was different from the law as amended` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
        WHEN `a declaration as to the previous state of the law` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`
    WHEN `something else` THEN `section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows`

-- src:430 | 45 (1) The repeal of an enactment in whole or in part shall not be deemed to be or to involve a declaration that the enactment was previously in force or was considered by Parliament or other body or person by whom the enactment was enacted to have been previously in force.
-- src:431 | Amendment does not imply change in law
-- src:432 | (2) The amendment of an enactment shall not be deemed to be or to involve a declaration that the law under that enactment was or was considered by Parliament or other body or person by whom the enactment was enacted to have been different from the law as it is under the enactment as amended.
-- src:433 | Repeal does not declare previous law
-- src:434 | (3) The repeal or amendment of an enactment in whole or in part shall not be deemed to be or to involve any declaration as to the previous state of the law.
-- src:435 | Judicial construction not adopted
-- src:436 | (4) A re-enactment, revision, consolidation or amendment of an enactment shall not be deemed to be or to involve an adoption of the construction that has by judicial decision or otherwise been placed on the language used in the enactment or on similar language.
@ref Interpretation Act s 45 (src:430-436)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 45 says what is not deemed to follow from each named act and does not say whether anything else follows"
